WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:08.848
Ever fixed the same error twice? Again remembers what you've tried, so you can pick up where you left off.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.922
Here, the administrator check already passed. The problem is starting the worker. Again brings back the earlier failed attempts.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:30.106
It keeps the outcome honest: worker startup was fixed, but the later trace was still unresolved.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:41.800
Same error, different situation. If the administrator check failed, the next step changes. Context matters.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:48.245
Switch memory off, and there's no pretend answer. Again says the history isn't available.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.023
Now let's teach it something. In this fictional example, the browser is using the wrong port.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.549
Save what you tried and what happened. Moss indexes the note for your browser session.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:15.830
Next time, ask in your own words. Moss finds the note, and Again asks whether those same conditions apply.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:28.244
You can inspect the sources, retrieved IDs, and real timings. No mystery answers.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.558
Again. Stop repeating failed fixes.
